/**

@page page_exahype_programmers_guide_action_sets How to define what a numerical scheme (or plotter or grid setup) does

\tableofcontents

The @ref page_exahype_programmers_guide_new_solver "introduce a new numerical scheme"
page shows how a Solver.NumericalScheme (or Solver.GridConstruction, or
Solver.Plotter) adds data to a solver and ensures that these data are also 
tied to the mesh properly.
This is all about static setups.
On this page, we discuss how to add dynamic behaviour.


ExaHyPE's current rewrite uses task graphs to model all behaviour.
You find the prototype of such a task graph in 
@ref exahype.api.fv.RusanovWithExplicitEuler.construct_output().
In general, any construct_output() from a numerical scheme, plot strategy
or mesh setup is responsible for returning a task graph
which describes what is to be done in this step.



## Construct the task graph


~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
        reconstruction_task        = peano4.api.taskgraph.Task(name=f"{self._solver.name}_Reconstruct and apply BCs",    entity=peano4.api.taskgraph.Task.GridEntity.CELL)
        update_cell_task           = peano4.api.taskgraph.Task(name=f"{self._solver.name}_Update cell",                  entity=peano4.api.taskgraph.Task.GridEntity.CELL)
        project_on_faces_task      = peano4.api.taskgraph.Task(name=f"{self._solver.name}_Project on faces",             entity=peano4.api.taskgraph.Task.GridEntity.CELL)
        compute_cfl_condition_task = peano4.api.taskgraph.Task(name=f"{self._solver.name}_Compute global CFL condition", entity=peano4.api.taskgraph.Task.GridEntity.CELL)

        update_cell_task.add_dependency(reconstruction_task)
        project_on_faces_task.add_dependency(update_cell_task)
        compute_cfl_condition_task.add_dependency(update_cell_task)

        time_step.add_task(reconstruction_task)
        time_step.add_task(update_cell_task)
        time_step.add_task(project_on_faces_task)
        time_step.add_task(compute_cfl_condition_task)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The CFL condition has a task of its own: The update task's action set
(exahype2.api.fv.actionsets.UpdateCell) stores the maximum eigenvalue of
every patch it updates in the cell. The task "Compute global CFL condition"
(exahype2.api.fv.actionsets.ComputeGlobalCFLCondition) then reduces these
values and derives the next global time step size from them. It only
depends on the update, i.e. it can run in parallel to the projection onto
the faces.


